<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Montana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Montana is a state of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, stretching from the Rocky Mountains to the northern Great Plains. Once home to the Blackfeet, Crow, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> and other peoples, it saw gold rushes in the 1860s and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-little-bighorn">Battle of the Little Bighorn</a> in 1876, and became the 41st state in 1889. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blackfeet-reservation">Blackfeet Reservation</a> lies in its north-west, along the Canadian border.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/montana.jpg" alt="Montana" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N.a · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Montana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Isotope analysis of Anzick-1, a young boy buried in <b>Montana</b> with over 100 stone and bone artefacts stained with red ochre, suggests that mammoth made up about 35–40 per cent of his group’s diet.</blockquote><a href="/culture/clovis-culture">Clovis culture · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Women entered legislatures: Jeannette Rankin of <b>Montana</b> was elected to the United States Congress in 1916, and Nancy Astor became the first woman to take a seat in the British House of Commons in 1919.</blockquote><a href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement">Women's suffrage movement · Outcomes</a></li><li><blockquote>United States Army forces under Major Eugene Mortimer Baker attacked Piegan Blackfeet in <b>Montana</b> Territory, killing approximately 200 people, most of them women, children and older men.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Lakota, Northern Cheyenne and Arapaho warriors killed Lieutenant Colonel George Custer and some 268 soldiers in <b>Montana</b> Territory.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-25">25 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>President Abraham Lincoln signed the law organizing the Territory of <b>Montana</b>, an organized incorporated territory of the United States.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Today they live on the Siksika, Kainai and Piikani reserves in Alberta and the Blackfeet Reservation in <b>Montana</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/blackfoot-confederacy">Blackfoot Confederacy</a></li></ul></section>
